<article class="post-wrap">
  <header class="post-header">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="post-meta">Effective October 26, 2026</p>
  </header>

  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      Harthunter Consulting is the sole proprietorship of Tram Ngo, based in the United States. This policy explains what information I collect, why, and what I do with it. It covers both this website and the information nonprofit clients share with me during a consulting engagement.
    </p>

    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <p>
      This website has no contact form, no analytics, and sets no cookies of its own. If you reach out, I use what you send to reply and to do the work you hire me for. I do not sell information, and I do not share client documents with anyone outside the engagement without your permission, unless the law requires it.
    </p>

    <h2>What this website collects</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Server logs.</strong> This site is hosted by Netlify. Like any web host, Netlify records technical information about requests, including IP address, browser type, and which pages were requested. I use this only to keep the site running and secure.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Fonts.</strong> The site loads typefaces from Google Fonts, which means Google receives your IP address when a page loads. Google states that it does not use these requests to build advertising profiles.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>The chat assistant.</strong> The homepage includes a chat assistant provided by a third-party service. If you start a conversation, what you type is processed by that provider so it can reply, and I can read those conversations. Treat it like an email to a stranger: useful for a question about my services, not the place for confidential organizational details or anyone's personal information.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>What you send me directly.</strong> If you email, call, or connect on LinkedIn, I receive whatever you choose to include. That is the only information this site asks for.
    </p>

    <h2>What I collect during an engagement</h2>
    <p>
      Grant work runs on documents, and some of them are sensitive. Depending on the service, a client may share governance records, IRS determination letters, Form 990s, audited financials and budgets, board rosters and contact details, strategic plans, program descriptions, outcomes and evaluation data, past proposals and funder correspondence, and staff names and roles.
    </p>
    <p>
      I ask clients not to send personal information about the people their programs serve. Readiness assessments and proposals almost never need it. If a funder requires participant-level data, we will agree in advance on how it is handled.
    </p>

    <h2>How I use it</h2>
    <p>
      To respond to inquiries, assess fit, prepare proposals and agreements, perform the work you hired me to do, invoice and keep tax records, and meet professional and legal obligations. That is the whole list. I do not use client documents to train anything, and I do not use them for marketing. If I ever want to describe your project as a case study or name you as a client, I will ask first and you can say no.
    </p>

    <h2>Who else sees it</h2>
    <p>
      I run a solo practice, so the answer is almost always no one. The exceptions:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Service providers I use to do the work</strong>, such as email, cloud file storage, electronic signature, and payment processing. They handle information on my behalf under their own terms and may not use it for their own purposes.</li>
      <li><strong>Funders and partners you direct me to contact</strong>, and only the information needed for that submission.</li>
      <li><strong>Legal requirements</strong>, if I am compelled by law. If that ever happens and I am permitted to tell you, I will.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      I do not sell information, rent it, or trade it. There is no advertising on this site and no data broker in this picture.
    </p>

    <h2>How long I keep it</h2>
    <p>
      Client files are kept for the length of the engagement and for a reasonable period afterward, because grant cycles repeat and prior applications matter to the next one. Financial and tax records are kept as long as the law requires. Outside of those requirements, you can ask me to delete your documents and I will.
    </p>

    <h2>How it is protected</h2>
    <p>
      Documents are stored in access-controlled cloud storage with multi-factor authentication, shared through private links rather than public ones, and kept off shared or unsecured devices. No system is perfect, and anyone who claims otherwise is selling something, but I do not keep client material lying around in places it does not belong.
    </p>

    <h2>Your confidentiality agreement comes first</h2>
    <p>
      If you are a client, the confidentiality terms in our signed agreement govern our work together. Where this policy and that agreement differ, the agreement controls.
    </p>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <p>
      You can ask me what information I hold about you, ask for a copy, ask me to correct it, or ask me to delete it. Email <a href="mailto:tram@harthunterconsulting.com">tram@harthunterconsulting.com</a> and I will respond within 30 days. If you are in California, the European Economic Area, or the United Kingdom, you may have additional rights under your local law, and I will honor valid requests under those laws. I will not treat you differently for making a request.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      This site and these services are intended for nonprofit professionals. They are not directed to children, and I do not knowingly collect information from anyone under 13.
    </p>

    <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
    <p>
      This site links to places like LinkedIn and funder websites. Once you follow a link, you are under that site's privacy policy, not this one.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes, the updated version will appear here with a new effective date. Material changes affecting active clients will be communicated directly.
    </p>

    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>
      Email <a href="mailto:tram@harthunterconsulting.com">tram@harthunterconsulting.com</a> or call <a href="tel:+18083487260">(808) 348-7260</a>. If something here is unclear, ask. A privacy policy nobody understands is not doing its job.
    </p>
  </div>
</article>
